<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_Piinnok.xml        Watchers - WATCHER_CREATURES_MOD_1, first member (design §7)

  The piinnok, "the watching glass" (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/stillsand_bedazzle_review_2026-09-29.md
  row 2; admitted in stillsand_bedazzle_cast_2026-09-30.md, owned by this item). Invented name, Q11a:
  RM_ tier. ONE home: the Stillsand. Its RM_Stillsand roster row is STILLSAND_BEDAZZLE_CONTENT_1's
  to add (that item's own note), not this file's.

  Owner rulings 2026-10-03 (decision taken by question card):
    Q1 lives on deep sand only            -> mediumTerrains RM_DeepSand (FlowWorks), waterSeeker +
                                             waterCellCost so vanilla wander and pathing prefer it
    Q2 two pictures                       -> stationaryGraphicData = the peek pose, bodyGraphicData =
                                             the whole creature (seen only when it moves). NO
                                             swimmingGraphicData: on deep sand (IsWater) it would win
                                             over the stationary sprite in every state (design §5 trap)
    Q3 tamed always stays on deep sand    -> the kit's medium lock applies to tame and wild alike
    Q4 (hunting) superseded 2026-10-08    -> no flushing: a hidden one cannot be targeted, a visible one is an
                                             ordinary target, area damage kills it either way (owner, DEATH card)

  Cross-mod content, each guarded by MayRequire so this mod stands alone:
    RM_DeepSand (mandrake.rm.flowworks); the filter-feed extension (ships in mandrake.rm.biomes, where
    CreatureBehaviors and Stillsand are composed).

  🔴 ART PLACEHOLDER: no piinnok art exists (artpipe_state.py find piinnok: 0 hits of 20,592, sanity
  probe hawkbat found; 2026-10-06). These are vanilla Odyssey hermit-crab textures (every DLC is
  assumed present), the closest vanilla still/moving pair. Owed, one artpipe job: the peek pose (lens
  dome + sand rim, iris direction readable N/E/S), the whole-body move sprite, dessicated.

  Numbers marked PROVISIONAL are invented for this build; design §7 fixed only bodySize ~0.15,
  group 2-4, geophone >= ~2.5 within 14, flinch 6.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Piinnok</defName>
    <label>piinnok</label>
    <description>Half the glassy nubs poking out of a deep-sand field are not plants. They are the lenses of piinnok: sessile burrowers whose one exposed organ is a water-clear dome. In a land where nothing tracks the sun, the piinnok is the one thing that tracks anything, and what it tracks is you. Walk past a field and a few glints turn to follow; walk too close and they are gone, leaving only a neat dimple in the sand. They are harmless, and so fragile that almost anything kills them.

Their real value is as living geophones. When every lens in a field sinks at once and nothing is walking nearby, something large is moving under that sand.

A piinnok lives only in deep sand and will not stay anywhere else. Nothing can aim at one while it hides, but fire, a blast or acid over its dimple kills it outright. All it leaves is a small clouded lens.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.4</MoveSpeed>            <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <MarketValue>30</MarketValue>         <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>0</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>90</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <LeatherAmount>0</LeatherAmount>
      <Wildness>0.9</Wildness>              <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>head</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>1</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>HeadAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>true</ensureLinkedBodyPartsGroupAlwaysUsable>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Watchers.RM_WatcherExtension">
        <mediumTerrains>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.flowworks">RM_DeepSand</li>
        </mediumTerrains>
        <flinchRadius>6</flinchRadius>
        <watchRadius>14</watchRadius>
        <hideTicks>2500~7500</hideTicks>
        <hiddenHediff>RM_WatcherHidden</hiddenHediff>
        <signDef>RM_WatcherSign_SandDimple</signDef>
        <geophoneMinBodySize>2.5</geophoneMinBodySize>
        <maxWatchTicks>2500</maxWatchTicks>     <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
        <wanderChance>0.1</wanderChance>        <!-- PROVISIONAL: sessile, it rarely moves -->
        <maxLethalDamage>5</maxLethalDamage>    <!-- owner 2026-10-08: almost no damage destroys it -->
        <remainsDef>RM_WatcherRemains_Piinnok</remainsDef>
        <remainsCarries>   <!-- owner 2026-10-08: the remains carry its biosilica. Spawned beside the remains on death (C#, not a recipe: MayRequire does not gate a whole Operation/RecipeDef). -->
          <RM_Biosilica MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">3</RM_Biosilica>   <!-- PROVISIONAL count; no grade above RM_Biosilica exists -->
        </remainsCarries>
        <emergeWhenFoodBelow>0.25</emergeWhenFoodBelow>
      </li>
      <!-- It strains the deep sand it lives in (the likka likka's shipped filter-feed stack). -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_FilterFeedExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.biomes">
        <feedTerrainDefNames>
          <li>RM_DeepSand</li>
        </feedTerrainDefNames>
        <beginBelowFoodPercent>0.6</beginBelowFoodPercent>   <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
        <foodPercentPerBout>0.3</foodPercentPerBout>         <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
        <boutDurationTicks>600</boutDurationTicks>
        <searchRadius>6</searchRadius>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <race>
      <body>BeetleLike</body>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <baseBodySize>0.15</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.02</baseHealthScale>    <!-- owner 2026-10-08 "almost no damage": an adult dies at 150 x 0.02 = 3 damage -->
      <baseHungerRate>0.06</baseHungerRate>      <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <useMeatFrom>Megaspider</useMeatFrom>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <!-- Deep sand is IsWater to the engine (FlowWorks RM_DeepSand carries the Water tag). waterSeeker
           lets vanilla wander use it despite avoidWander; waterCellCost replaces its pathCost 300 for
           this race (Pawn_PathFollower, PathFinderCostTuning; design §1). Walrus/sea turtle value. -->
      <waterSeeker>true</waterSeeker>
      <waterCellCost>1</waterCellCost>
      <lifeExpectancy>6</lifeExpectancy>         <!-- PROVISIONAL -->
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li><def>AnimalBaby</def><minAge>0</minAge></li>
        <li><def>AnimalJuvenile</def><minAge>0.1</minAge></li>
        <li><def>AnimalAdult</def><minAge>0.25</minAge></li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalUncommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_Piinnok</defName>
    <label>piinnok</label>
    <labelPlural>piinnok</labelPlural>
    <race>RM_Piinnok</race>
    <combatPower>3</combatPower>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.05</ecoSystemWeight>
    <canArriveManhunter>false</canArriveManhunter>
    <wildGroupSize>2~4</wildGroupSize>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/HermitCrabA</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <stationaryGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/HermitCrabA_Stationary</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.3</drawSize>
        </stationaryGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/Dessicated_HermitCrabA</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.3</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/HermitCrabA</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.38</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <stationaryGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/HermitCrabA_Stationary</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.38</drawSize>
        </stationaryGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/Dessicated_HermitCrabA</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.38</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/HermitCrabA</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.45</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <stationaryGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/HermitCrabA_Stationary</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.45</drawSize>
        </stationaryGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/HermitCrab/Dessicated_HermitCrabA</texPath>
          <drawSize>0.45</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
